# gap-prepare-milestone-convergence-test-fixture-pollutes-production-tree (2026-07-31): safety-net
# only — the real fix is the test itself no longer writing outside its own scratch dir. If a test
# process is killed before its `finally { cleanup(...) }` runs, these interrupted-run orphans are
# what's left behind: docs/plans/M<6-digit>-*.md and milestones/M<6-digit>/ (real milestone IDs
# never reach 6 digits, so this cannot collide with a genuine milestone).
docs/plans/M9[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-*.md
milestones/M9[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/
# Same class, second source found 2026-07-31: prepare-milestone-preparation-e2e.test.mjs uses a
# FIXED milestoneId 'M997' (not random) for its own Plan-file/milestones scratch — its own
# `finally` cleanup exists but this test currently fails (pre-existing, unrelated to any change in
# this commit — confirmed via git stash) before reaching a passing assertion in some runs, leaving
# the same shape of orphan behind.
docs/plans/M997-*.md
milestones/M997/
